"""Write bounded lead verdicts from inspected raw evidence; no score-to-verdict rule."""
import csv
import json
from pathlib import Path

B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
Q=list(csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf-8')))
V={
'H001':('REFUTED','','','','The only retained dip, s81 BTJD 3518.706, is the start of a descending trend immediately before a gap and large flux step. The full s54/s81 SAP curves show broad evolving baselines, not a resolved repeat.','Refutation applies to the selected dip claim; a different hidden eclipse is not excluded.','Independent high-resolution light curve of the s81 interval or a new clean conjunction window.'),
'H002':('CONFIRMED','59.03','2040.0819','37','Raw SAP has complete flat-bottom declines in s27 and s101, ~35–38 ppt over ~2.7 d. Locally fitted centers are BTJD 2040.0819 and 4106.0797; their 35-cycle separation gives 59.0285 d, 1.2 Gaia formal period sigma above 58.9973 d. Two further occasions corroborate N35 without precision centers: s94 has a post-gap low state and sharp egress near 3871.3, matching the predicted center 3869.966 plus ~1.35 d half-duration; s103 has ingress near 4163.8 and egress near 4166.3 bracketing predicted center 4165.108, with the middle lost to a gap. N34 predicts a clean null in s13 and N36 a mostly quiet s94 window near 3876.52; other nearby aliases differ from Gaia by >60 formal sigma. The Gaia B conjunction differs by 0.0007 phase. Independent TESSCut aperture of s27 gives 35.41 ppt from the same photons, and WCS difference flux peaks 0.242 pixel from the target; all Gaia neighbors within 60 arcsec are too faint under approximate G-band total-disappearance bounds.','Period is a rounded two-complete-event estimate supported by two partial occasions, conditional on N35; no calibrated period error. Other screened shallow dips are not assigned to the same eclipse kind. The WCS/neighbor assessment is bounded and uses approximate G-to-TESS flux.','Obtain another complete same-kind eclipse and independent photometry for a precision ephemeris.'),
'H003':('REFUTED','','','','Flagged s33, s87 and s98 dips are gap/step or changing-baseline segments in SAP; s98 is a long decline through a gap. Full sectors show jagged/broad variability, with no repeated resolved eclipse at the Gaia conjunctions.','This refutes the selected flagged/eclipse interpretation, not every possible unobserved eclipse.','Check a clean future conjunction with a stable aperture if this variable merits follow-up.'),
'H004':('REFUTED','','','','The s26 retained dips are monotonic rising segments, s80 is a gap step, and s40/s79 are brightenings. Across five full SAP sectors the dominant signal is broad variation; no repeated eclipse is isolated.','The brightening may be real variability, with source and physical mechanism unassigned.','Investigate the broad variability separately if of interest.'),
'H005':('PLAUSIBLE','','','','One shallow s94 depression at BTJD ~3875.09 sits near a gap and on a changing baseline. Earlier full SAP sectors do not show a secure matched event. The s95 raw flux has pathological near-zero stretches despite quality-zero samples, so it cannot certify a null.','Eclipse shape, recurrence, period and source attribution are insecure; 206 other-CCD flags are a common-mode hint only.','Recover a clean second event with usable pre/post baseline, then test pixel attribution.'),
'H006':('PLAUSIBLE','','','','In s76 a broad flag is part of a rising step/brightening, while a separate narrow trough near BTJD 3388.84 is visible. Clean windows at the Gaia-period extrapolations in s75 (~3342.97) and s81 (~3526.47) lack comparable narrow troughs; an earlier s41 window is also quiet.','This disfavors repetition at that assumed Gaia phase, but the single trough is not securely classified; another period or non-eclipse variability remains possible. No event depth or timing precision is claimed.','Seek another isolated narrow trough and test its period before source attribution.'),
'H007':('REFUTED','','','','The s59 dip flag is a gap recovery. The s74 selected dip is the low state before a large broad brightening, and its brightening flag captures that rise. Full ten-sector SAP context has variable baseline and no isolated repeated eclipse.','The broad brightening may have an astrophysical cause; eclipse refutation is limited to this candidate interpretation.','Analyze the brightening morphology separately if pursued.'),
'H008':('PLAUSIBLE','','','79','The s70 SAP event is a complete ~79 ppt flat-bottom eclipse with local fitted center BTJD 3232.1065. s92 descends around BTJD 3814.56–3814.79 and remains low to ~3815.3, consistent with another eclipse, but its egress is lost to quality-bit 1073741824 censoring; its fitted center is model-dependent. An 18-cycle assignment gives ~32.392 d, close to Gaia 32.39435 d, and the Gaia B conjunction is 0.0228 phase away. Other N15–N21 aliases have no independent sensitive nulls in cached sectors. TESSCut s70 aperture recovers 63.97 ppt from the same photons; difference flux peaks 0.036 pixel from target. A G=12.153 neighbor at 54.66 arcsec is in principle flux-capable but at a different WCS position.','Two-event cycle count remains untested by an independent clean occasion; no established period or precision epoch in result row. Source attribution is supported but lacks full PRF deblend.','Observe a complete third same-kind event to settle cycle count and timing; deblend if publication depends on attribution.'),
'H009':('REFUTED','','','','s25 flagged dips ride smooth long-term variable trends; s79 dip is a gap/step. Full eight-sector SAP curves are dominated by broad swings, with no isolated repeated eclipse.','Selected eclipse interpretation is refuted; alternative variability is not classified.','Characterize broad variability separately if useful.'),
'H010':('REFUTED','','','','s6 and s34 flags follow broad quasi-periodic variability, with s34 interrupted by a gap; their shapes and context do not support a matched eclipse. Full five-sector SAP curves show rolling modulation rather than stable flat-bottom events.','This refutes the screened eclipse interpretation but does not identify the physical source of variability.','Compare independent photometry if the non-eclipse variability is investigated.'),
}

fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
rows=[]
for q in Q:
    sid=q['sample_id'];tic=q['tic'];verdict,period,epoch,depth,evidence,limit,nextcheck=V[sid]
    raw=json.loads((B/tic/'raw-inspection.json').read_text())
    sectors=[s['sector'] for s in raw['sectors'] if 'path' in s]
    report=(f'# {sid} — TIC {tic}\n\n'
      f'Physical verdict: **{verdict}**. Bounded review: **COMPLETE**. Catalogue novelty: **UNKNOWN**; four scoped VizieR gates remained unqueried after the positive control timed out, so bounded local nonmatches are not clearance.\n\n'
      f'Gaia DR3 source {q["gaia_dr3"]}, SB1 period {float(q["gaia_period_days"]):.5f} d. Frozen stratum `{q["sample_stratum"]}`; sample position is not scientific rank. Cached quality-zero raw SAP sectors: {", ".join(map(str,sectors))}.\n\n'
      f'## Deciding evidence\n\n{evidence}\n\n'
      f'## Limits and next check\n\n{limit} {nextcheck}\n\n'
      f'## Reproducibility\n\n`raw-inspection.json` verifies the bulk JSON and each used FITS SHA-256 and records representative screening windows. `raw-windows.png` shows flagged raw windows; `orbit-context.png` and `.json` show full cached-sector SAP and Gaia conjunction predictions. These predictions are not event timings. Source packets under `../../source-packets/{tic}/sources.json` carry frozen target/orbit/fold receipts. `../../shared-catalogues/target-evidence.json` holds bounded novelty evidence; a failed remote query is unknown. Scripts in this batch reproduce lead artifacts.\n')
    if sid=='H002': report+='\nThe result epoch BTJD 2040.0819 labels the deeper sampled eclipse kind as a provisional primary; no stellar primary or opposite eclipse kind has been established. `local-fits.json`, `cycle-coverage.json`, `alias-tests.json`, and helper attribution artifacts document the measured events, alias checks, alternative aperture and WCS difference image. The s94/s103 partial contacts corroborate recurrence but are not fitted precision centers.\n'
    if sid=='H008': report+='\n`local-fits.json`, `cycle-coverage.json`, `alias-tests.json`, and helper attribution artifacts document the complete s70 event and censored s92 event. The conditional 18-cycle estimate is intentionally omitted from the result period field.\n'
    if sid in ('H005','H006','H008'):
        avail=json.loads((B/'sector-availability.json').read_text()).get(tic,{})
        report+=f"\nCurrent TESScut sector inventory returned HTTP {avail.get('http_status','UNKNOWN')} with sectors {avail.get('available_sectors','UNKNOWN')}; it lists no additional sector beyond the cached set. The query receipt and response hash are in `sector-availability.json` and `sector-availability.raw`.\n"
    if sid in ('H005','H006'):report+='\n`repeat-windows.json` and `.png` test selected Gaia-period repeat opportunities; nulls apply only to that clock and phase.\n' if sid=='H006' else ''
    (B/tic/'REPORT.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
    rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=q['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=verdict,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status='UNKNOWN',period_days=period,period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd=epoch,depth_ppt=depth,limitations=limit,next_check=nextcheck,report=str((B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve())))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
    writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);writer.writeheader();writer.writerows(rows)
print({v:sum(r['physical_verdict']==v for r in rows) for v in sorted(set(r['physical_verdict'] for r in rows))})
